[32m+[m[32m## Δ[m
[32m+[m[32m  A syntax-highlighting pager for git.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  _(This project is at a very early stage, but please feel free to open issues.)_[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Installation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### 1. Rust development environment.[m
[32m+[m[32m  See https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### 2. Clone this repo.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### 3. Build the executable:[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```sh[m
[32m+[m[32m  cd delta[m
[32m+[m[32m  cargo build[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  This creates an executable inside the repo at `target/debug/delta`. Copy or symlink this executable to somewhere on your shell[m
[32m+[m[32m  `$PATH`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  If you're not sure what that means, ignore it, and use[m
[32m+[m[32m  `/path/to/delta/target/debug/delta | less -R` in the next step.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### 4. Configure git to use delta:[m
[32m+[m[32m  Edit your `~/.gitconfig`:[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  [core][m
[32m+[m[32m      pager = delta | less -R[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  Alternatively, run this command:[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m[32m  git config --global core.pager 'delta | less -R'[m
[32m+[m[32m  ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll git commands that display diff output should now display syntax-highlighted output. For example:[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `git diff`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `git show`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `git log -p`[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `git stash show -p`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Credit[m
[32m+[m[32m  https://github.com/trishume/syntect<br>[m
[32m+[m[32m  https://github.com/sharkdp/bat[m

